{"kind":"assert","text":"Ruling on request 236a56a0, JP1 controls: keep the Page result, and\nrun the MCP18 mutant once. Do not repeat Page.\n\n1. The Page control did its job. The mutant restored the missing-pin\n   fallback, and the one intended case went red at join.test.ts:55,\n   where `rejects.toThrow` met a promise that resolved. The other case\n   passed. That is the distinction that the control exists to show.\n   The wrong needle is a fault of the controller, not of the head.\n2. Conditions. Seal the failed unit as it is and take the independent\n   readback. The review note says that controller 96372c4e exited 2 on\n   a wrong needle, and it names the default and JSON reports that show\n   the red case. It does not call that window a pass. The checker\n   judges this evidence at review. If the checker asks for the Page\n   control again, it runs then.\n3. Before you allocate the MCP18 run, one source reader confirms that\n   its needle is text that Vitest prints when the mutant takes effect.\n   A `rejects` or `resolves` assertion prints Vitest's own sentence and\n   not the business error. That check reads source and runs nothing.\n4. Main holds at af3badef through the END of the MCP18 window. The\n   hold ends at that END, whatever the result. If the controller stops\n   at its classifier again with a distinct child, do not rerun. Seal,\n   report and ask.\n\nThe slot goes to S1 after that END.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}